  The weekly meter reached <strong|30% remaining on 12 November 2026 at 13:46
  UTC>. The parent and its subagents have stopped mathematical work. This
  handoff covers all 241 included chapters, existing external suppliers,
  independent review, source/meaning audits, bibliography, Section 2,
  notation/order and symbolic index. <strong|The whole proof remains
  incomplete.> Final integration F01 is reserved for the user's later
  request; this parent must not resume automatically.

  Mathematical snapshot: <hlink|<verbatim|9b879ee64bdf2d5cfda8fd72e3bfd03cd53a980b>|https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/commit/9b879ee64bdf2d5cfda8fd72e3bfd03cd53a980b>.
  The 872-page PDF and chapter hashes are frozen at that commit. The final
  handoff commit and draft PR are linked from the <hlink|parent claim-release
  comment in issue26|https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/issues/26#issuecomment-6825417454>.
  Start from that final released commit on
  <verbatim|codex/existence-monograph>, which adds these task links and
  contracts without changing the mathematics. Ready scopes activate only
  after that release comment; G04/G06 remain blocked on their named
  prerequisites and F01 remains reserved. No package document is a lock. See
  the <hlink|external ownership snapshot|external-claims.tm> and recheck live
  claims.

  Start with <hlink|the common contract|COMMON-CONTRACT.tm>, <hlink|the
  copyable agent prompt|AGENT-PROMPT.tm>, and <hlink|known open
  interfaces|known-open-edges.tm>. Every author package needs a separate
  independent reviewer of both mathematics and Lean correspondence. The
  coverage inventory assigns every included chapter exactly once; local
  bounded passes do not exempt a chapter from dependency closure.

  <section|Mathematical coverage, audit and
  repair><label|mathematical-coverage-audit-and-repair>

  Each package owns only its named chapters and its report directory.
  Authoring may begin with precise draft inputs; global closure cannot be
  claimed until those inputs are proved and matched. Split an overlarge
  package at a mathematical interface before work, recording disjoint scopes
  in the live issues.

