    <item><hlink|Issue34|https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/issues/34>:
    branch moments and trace washout; owned by its external claimant.

    <item><hlink|Issue37|https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/issues/37>:
    independent clean-source build; do not repeat its work or overstate
    earlier artifact evidence.

    <item><hlink|Issue22|https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/issues/22>:
    canonical running-coupling extraction; G02 reuses this unit and addresses
    its review.
  </itemize-minus>

  External delivery still needs exact-version integration and independent
  review. No parent handoff can release another contributor's claim. Recheck
  all live claims; respect the contributing human's account and submission
  restrictions.

  <section|Dispatch and completion><label|dispatch-and-completion>

  After the parent release, C authors plus G01/G03/G05 can start disjoint
  audits. C12/C13/C14 and C05 have known common-data joins documented in the
  interface ledger; this is a useful priority, not permission to neglect the
  remaining chapters. G05 provides a notation/order contract before authors
  finish local polishing. Arrange independent reviewers after each author
  delivers its final hash.

  G04 writes the actual argument outline with verified historical references.
  G06 tests the union of all theorem-level input/output ledgers, including
  the external trace results and final same-witness assembly. A package-level
  cycle is not necessarily a proof cycle; check the actual statements and
  choices. Every genuine new gap gets a bounded owned repair, never an
  invented premise.

  F01 is reserved for the user's later request. Finishing the other packages
  does not authorize the stopped parent to resume. Material changes during
  that final pass need renewed independent review and G06 final-hash signoff.

  Read <hlink|newly merged shared evidence|upstream-evidence.tm>, including
  the OS, Gaussian/nonlinear/rank interface, Balaban and running-coupling
  review notes. These upstream inputs may be newer than the frozen branch;
  preserve their ownership.

